   "evidence": "HEAD executes 'if (result.kind !== \"moved\") return \"pending\"; store.markLeaseLost(repo, ref); return \"superseded\";' at lines 132\u2013134 without inspecting result.tip. markLeaseLost sets confirmed_state to 'lost' and clears every intent column. A moved result merely establishes that the tip changed; it does not establish supersession, and the base claim client explicitly permits malformed records in moved outcomes. Lease recovery is absent at base. The later commit assigns 'tip = result.tip' and applies malformed/equivalence/generation/holder/run classification; both temporary regressions pass with confirmed ownership and the release intent retained."
